  "name": "Not All Graphs Are Maps: A Task-Agnostic Exploration Framework for Mobile GUI Navigation",
  "notes": "The controlled cohort has 84 tasks across six apps; the broader inventory spans 20 apps. Main results use human destination labels. DroidTask and SPA-Bench are converted to navigation-only protocols. Some comparison cells received another graph condition’s memory, with sensitivity analyses reported. Cross-family runs differ in app versions, state and denominators. A small stale-graph probe does not establish robustness. Models, code, artifacts and performance were not independently reproduced.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-15",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "TAG-Nav supplies Android GUI agents with destination and route memory distilled from offline app exploration. DestBench measures arrival at a reference pre-action screen, separately from downstream task execution.",
  "topics": [
    "mobile-navigation",
    "memory",
    "evaluation"
  ],
